            "notes": "I don't have strong feelings on power for this round.  [Lunar Leap](item_dd41728d-7997-487f-93f5-859b3e9d0c84) feels like it's got a lot of potential since you can just leap nonstop and forever be generating 5% of your HP as overhealth.  [Surge Protector](item_5a653c7a-e156-449c-905b-83a1a54e7f93) has potential if your team needs some help living, but it doesn't do a hell of a lot.\n\nUltimately though,  [Moon Landing](item_cc4f210b-31e1-47b2-8400-325afcc4892b) is probably the most health per second that you can generate. Hitting 2 target with jump pack damage is giving you 14% of your health every 2.5 seconds and you can basically sustain forever on point.\n\nWe do have  [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f)  but in a pinch you can Primal and never die with a 1 second leap cooldown and ~2k health...you can self heal around 250hp a second during Primal by just leaping on people over and over. That's not even including  [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) which also heals you 60hp a second during Primal.\n\nMake no mistake though, you are much much squishier during Primal than normal. No bubbles, no overhealth generation from electric damage. ONLY use Primal if you'd die otherwise.\n\nYou can also substitute [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) for [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) if enemy healing is an issue.",
